Fixed 2026-11-19, before any result of this definition was read (borg-reborn-rs#690, PR #702). Pilot (RULES 16);
small and medium (starts 1-360) after this gate: locally the rule never fires on classes-18, so the pilot shows
safety only, and the owner asked for the measurement.
Gate:
- no config_error; one binary; each arm's value in borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays;
- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn bursts classified and key outliers listed;
- death bundles reproduced;
- in ctl, no "# Walking out of a slower crowd" note.
Report per arm and per class, from every game's messages:
- deaths and causes, final and maximum level, deepest level; deaths to a slower or never-moving killer
  (monster.txt speed below 110, or NEVER_MOVE);
- paired rescued and newly killed against ctl;
- "# Walking out of a slower crowd" notes per game, by kind (exit grids or open grids) and distance;
- deaths within 500 game turns of such a note;
- games with "Possibility of being surrounded" at danger at or above the HP for 20 or more thinks on one grid.
Context: local classes-18 (100,000 turns), the two arms play identical keys (18/18); on the case's own build the
rule turns borg-cemetery#78's death into a survival.
